From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Druchenko <bananos@dev.co.ua>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:43:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] b43: N-PHY: per-rate TX power on radio 2057 rev 13

The adjusted power table (tables 26/27, offset 64) holds each rate's
power below the TX power control target, as brcmsmac fills it from
tx_power_offset[]; b43 never filled tx_power_offset[], so every rate
went at the target. On radio 2057 rev 13, fill it from b43's PPR (the
SROM's cck2gpo, ofdm2gpo, mcs2gpo, CDD and STBC offsets, capped by the
regulatory limit and the user's TX power), whose rates are in the order
of its first 52 entries. Drop the fixed 13.5 dBm target of that radio:
the target is the PPR maximum again.

On an ASUS RT-N12 D1 (channel 11, HT20, ht=1): TX retries 12% (was
27%), 12.1 / 19.6 Mbit/s AP->client / client->AP at 20 dBm, 12.1 / 22.7
with the TX power set to 14 dBm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 24 +++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
index e824089..66cacc1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -4278,15 +4278,23 @@ static void b43_nphy_tx_power_ctl_setup(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 	if (ppr_max) {
 		target[0] = ppr_max;
 		target[1] = ppr_max;
+
+		/*
+		 * The per-rate powers relative to the target, for the adjusted
+		 * power table (as brcmsmac's tx_power_offset[]): b43's PPR
+		 * rates are in the order of its first 52 entries (CCK, OFDM,
+		 * OFDM CDD, MCS 20 MHz SISO, CDD, STBC, SDM). 40 MHz: none yet.
+		 * So far only on radio 2057 rev 13, where it was tested.
+		 */
+		memset(nphy->tx_power_offset, 0, sizeof(nphy->tx_power_offset));
+		for (i = 0; phy->radio_ver == 0x2057 && phy->radio_rev == 13 &&
+			    i < B43_PPR_RATES_NUM &&
+			    i < ARRAY_SIZE(nphy->tx_power_offset); i++) {
+			u8 r = nphy->tx_pwr_max_ppr.__all_rates[i];
+
+			nphy->tx_power_offset[i] = r && r < ppr_max ? ppr_max - r : 0;
+		}
 	}
-	/*
-	 * Radio 2057 rev 13: wl 5.110's target on the ASUS RT-N12 D1, 0x36
-	 * (13.5 dBm), where ppr_max gives 20 dBm. The per-rate powers of the
-	 * NVRAM (ofdm2gpo, mcs2gpo) are not applied yet; until they are, this
-	 * keeps the internal PA out of compression.
-	 */
-	if (phy->radio_ver == 0x2057 && phy->radio_rev == 13)
-		target[0] = target[1] = 0x36;
 
 	if (dev->phy.rev >= 3) {
 		if (sprom->fem.ghz2.tssipos)
